s across the SDK docs log in with the iggy/iggy root credentials. These only exist when the server is started with the default-credentials flag (or IGGY_ROOT_USERNAME/IGGY_ROOT_PASSWORD set) on its first boot. Otherwise root gets a generated password and the samples fail with InvalidCredentials:"},"2487":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-55","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#prerequisites","content":"--fresh wipes the local data directory, so an existing server with different stored credentials is re-initialized. This setup is for development only."},"2488":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-56","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#connection-string","content":"Connection strings are supported by the Rust, Python, C++, and PHP SDKs. They provide a compact way to configure the client, including the transport protocol, credentials, server address, and options."},"2489":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-57","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#connection-string","content":"Format:"},"2490":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-58","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#connection-string","content":"Transport selection via scheme:"},"2491":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-59","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#connection-string","content":"Scheme"},"2492":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-60","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#connection-string","content":"Transport"},"2493":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-61","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#connection-string","content":"iggy://"},"2494":{"id":"/docs/sdk/introduction-62","page_id":"/docs/sdk/introduction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/introduction#connection-string","cont