/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"There is no default secret. With the secrets left empty, each server start mints a random signing key, so issued tokens do not survive a restart and are valid only on the node that issued them. If you configure a secret, set it through the environment (IGGY_HTTP_JWT_ENCODING_SECRET / IGGY_HTTP_JWT_DECODING_SECRET), never commit it, and use a long random value."},"2734":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-164","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwt","content":"In cluster mode the secret has an extra role: a configured secret, identical on every node, makes bearer tokens valid cluster-wide and activates follower-to-primary HTTP forwarding. With cluster.auth enabled the JWT key is instead derived from the cluster PSK. Without either, tokens are node-local and forwarding stays disabled."},"2735":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-165","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwttrusted_issuers","content":"Opt-in trust of external token issuers for application-to-application authentication. With none configured, the listener accepts only self-issued HS256 tokens."},"2736":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-166","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwttrusted_issuers","content":"issuer, audience, and jwks_url are required per entry. user_id is the non-zero iggy user every token from that issuer is remapped onto. It defaults to 0 (root), which is rejected, so set it explicitly."},"2737":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-167","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpjwttrusted_issuers","content":"Enabling an issuer opens an outbound JWKS fetch that is reachable before a token's signature is verified: a token naming the issuer with an unknown key id can trigger a fetch to jwks_url. The target is fixed (not attacker-chosen), concurrent misses coalesce onto one fetch, and repeats are rate-limited to one outbound request per issuer per short window. The same window bounds how quickly a freshly rotated signing key is picked up."},"2738":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-168","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"Key"},"2739":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-169","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"Default"},"2740":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-170","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"Description"},"2741":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-171","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"enabled"},"2742":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-172","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"true"},"2743":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-173","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"Expose Prometheus metrics."},"2744":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-174","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"endpoint"},"2745":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-175","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"\"/metrics\""},"2746":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-176","page_id":"/docs/server/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/server/configuration#httpmetrics","content":"Metrics path. Must start with /."},"2747":{"id":"/docs/server/configuration-177","page_id":"