","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"table"},"3579":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-24","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"match_all"},"3580":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-25","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"Elasticsearch query DSL applied on each poll"},"3581":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-26","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"polling_interval"},"3582":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-27","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"string"},"3583":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-28","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"\"10s\""},"3584":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-29","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"Delay before each poll cycle"},"3585":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-30","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"batch_size"},"3586":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-31","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"integer"},"3587":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-32","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"100"},"3588":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-33","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"Maximum documents fetched per poll"},"3589":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-34","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"timestamp_field"},"3590":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-35","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"string"},"3591":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-36","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"none"},"3592":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-37","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"Document field used for incremental polling"},"3593":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-38","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"A custom query must be a structured object. In TOML that means nested tables (an inline JSON string won't work):"},"3594":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-39","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#plugin-config-options","content":"Alternatively, set plugin_config_format = \"json\" and provide the plugin config as JSON, as the crate's own config example does."},"3595":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-40","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#how-polling-works","content":"Each cycle the connector waits polling_interval, then runs a search against index with the configured query, size = batch_size, sorted ascending by timestamp_field (@timestamp when unset). Every document's _source becomes one JSON message."},"3596":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-41","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#how-polling-works","content":"When timestamp_field is set, the query is also filtered to documents whose timestamp is greater than the newest one seen so far, so already-processed documents are not fetched again. Without a timestamp_field there is no incremental cursor and each poll returns the first batch_size matching documents."},"3597":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-42","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#state","content":"State is managed by the connectors runtime, not by the connector itself. Along with each batch of produced messages, the connector returns its progress (last poll timestamp plus document, poll, and error counters). The runtime persists it atomically to a per-connector file, source_<key>.state, under the [state] path from the runtime config (default local_state). On restart the runtime hands the saved state back to the connector, which resumes polling from the last processed timestamp."},"3598":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch-43","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/elasticsearch#state","content":"State persistence requires no plugin configuration. To reset the connector's position, stop the runtime and delete the state file."},"3599":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","type":"page","content":"InfluxDB Source","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Connectors","Sources"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb"},"3600":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-0","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","content":"Poll InfluxDB on an interval and produce the resulting rows into an Iggy stream, on both InfluxDB V2 and V3."},"3601":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-1","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"3602":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-2","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb#common-options","content":"Common Options"},"3603":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-3","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb#cursor-based-polling","content":"Cursor-Based Polling"},"3604":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-4","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb#payload-formats","content":"Payload Formats"},"3605":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-5","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","content":"The InfluxDB source connector polls InfluxDB on an interval and produces the resulting rows as messages into an Iggy stream. It supports both InfluxDB V2 (OSS 2.x / Cloud, Flux queries) and InfluxDB V3 (Core / Enterprise, SQL queries), selected with the version option. A timestamp cursor stored in persistent connector state tracks the position, so restarts resume where they left off."},"3606":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-6","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","content":"This page is a curated subset of the documentation. The canonical reference, including the full cursor semantics and stuck-timestamp handling, is the upstream influxdb_source README in the apache/iggy repository."},"3607":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-7","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb#configuration","content":"InfluxDB V2 takes an org and a Flux query. V3 takes a db and a SQL query:"},"3608":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-8","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb#configuration","content":"Omitting version defaults to \"v2\" for backward compatibility. The query template must contain the $cursor placeholder (enforced at startup). $limit is strongly recommended so batch_size bounds each query. V3 queries also need OFFSET $offset unless stuck-batch detection is disabled."},"3609":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-9","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb#common-options","content":"Option"},"3610":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-10","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb#common-options","content":"Type"},"3611":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-11","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb#common-options","content":"Default"},"3612":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-12","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb#common-options","content":"Description"},"3613":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb-13","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sources/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sou