each consume cycle bulk-indexes the batch of messages it receives. The connector performs no retries of its own. Failed batches are logged and counted."},"4061":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-39","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#index-mapping","content":"index_mapping is sent verbatim as the body of the create-index request, so it must be a structured object, not a JSON string embedded in TOML. Express it as nested TOML tables:"},"4062":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-40","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#payload-handling","content":"JSON payloads are indexed as documents directly."},"4063":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-41","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#payload-handling","content":"Raw payloads are parsed as JSON when possible, and wrapped as { \"data\": \"<base64>\", \"data_type\": \"raw\" } when that fails."},"4064":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-42","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#payload-handling","content":"Text payloads are wrapped as { \"text\": \"...\", \"data_type\": \"text\" }."},"4065":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-43","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#payload-handling","content":"Other payload formats are skipped with a warning."},"4066":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch-44","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/elasticsearch#payload-handling","content":"Each document is enriched with metadata fields before indexing: _iggy_offset, _iggy_stream, _iggy_topic, _iggy_partition, _iggy_timestamp, and _iggy_headers (when headers are present)."},"4067":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"page","content":"HTTP Sink","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Connectors","Sinks"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http"},"4068":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-0","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","content":"Deliver messages from Iggy streams to any HTTP endpoint, from webhooks and REST APIs to serverless functions."},"4069":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-1","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"4070":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-2","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Common Options"},"4071":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-3","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#batch-modes","content":"Batch Modes"},"4072":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-4","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#metadata-envelope","content":"Metadata Envelope"},"4073":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-5","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#authentication","content":"Authentication"},"4074":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-6","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#retry--delivery-semantics","content":"Retry & Delivery Semantics"},"4075":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-7","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#example-configurations","content":"Example Configurations"},"4076":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-8","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#webhook-slack","content":"Webhook (Slack)"},"4077":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-9","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#bulk-rest-api-ingestion","content":"Bulk REST API Ingestion"},"4078":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-10","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#iot--sensor-relay-binary-payloads","content":"IoT / Sensor Relay (binary payloads)"},"4079":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-11","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#deployment--performance","content":"Deployment & Performance"},"4080":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-12","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#known-limitations","content":"Known Limitations"},"4081":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-13","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","content":"The HTTP Sink connector consumes messages from Iggy streams and delivers them to any HTTP endpoint: webhooks, REST APIs, serverless functions, or SaaS integrations. This is the transport-level, generic HTTP connector. It's distinct from sinks such as Elasticsearch or Quickwit, which use HTTP internally to talk to one specific system. You bring the URL, headers, and batching strategy, and the sink handles transport, retries, and metadata wrapping."},"4082":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-14","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","content":"This page is a curated subset of the documentation. The canonical reference, including the full configuration table, deployment patterns, and performance analysis, is the upstream http_sink README in the apache/iggy repository."},"4083":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-15","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Option"},"4084":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-16","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Type"},"4085":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-17","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Default"},"4086":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-18","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Description"},"4087":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-19","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"url"},"4088":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-20","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"string"},"4089":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-21","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"required"},"4090":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-22","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Target URL for HTTP requests"},"4091":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-23","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"method"},"4092":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-24","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"string"},"4093":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-25","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"POST"},"4094":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-26","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"HTTP method: GET, HEAD, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE"},"4095":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-27","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"batch_mode"},"4096":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-28","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"string"},"4097":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-29","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"individual"},"4098":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-30","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"individual, ndjson, json_array, or raw"},"4099":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-31","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"include_metadata"},"4100":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-32","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"bool"},"4101":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-33","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"true"},"4102":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-34","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Wrap payload in metadata envelope"},"4103":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-35","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"headers"},"4104":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-36","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"table"},"4105":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-37","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"{}"},"4106":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-38","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Custom HTTP headers (e.g. Authorization)"},"4107":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-39","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"timeout"},"4108":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-40","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"string"},"4109":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-41","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"30s"},"4110":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-42","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Request timeout (e.g. 10s, 500ms)"},"4111":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-43","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"Further options cover retries (max_retries, retry_delay, retry_backoff_multiplier, max_retry_delay), success status codes, payload size limits, TLS, connection pooling, health checks, and verbose logging. See the upstream http_sink README for the full list with defaults."},"4112":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-44","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#common-options","content":"GET and HEAD are accepted but unusual for delivering data: the request still carries a body, which some servers reject. The sink logs a warning at startup when GET or HEAD is combined with a batch mode other than individual."},"4113":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-45","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#batch-modes","content":"The batch_mode option controls how messages from one poll cycle are delivered to the endpoint."},"4114":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-46","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#batch-modes","content":"individual (default): one HTTP request per message. Best for webhooks and endpoints that accept single events. With batch_length = 50, this produces 50 sequential round trips per poll cycle."},"4115":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-47","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#batch-modes","content":"ndjson: all messages in one request, newline-delimited JSON. Best for bulk-ingestion endpoints. Content-Type: application/x-ndjson."},"4116":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-48","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#batch-modes","content":"json_array: all messages as a single JSON array. Best for APIs that expect array payloads. Content-Type: application/json."},"4117":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-49","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#batch-modes","content":"raw: raw bytes, one request per message. For non-JSON payloads (Protobuf, FlatBuffers, binary). The metadata envelope is not applied. Content-Type: application/octet-stream."},"4118":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-50","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#batch-modes","content":"For production throughput with JSON-representable payloads, prefer ndjson or json_array, which collapse N round trips per poll cycle into one."},"4119":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-51","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#metadata-envelope","content":"When include_metadata = true (default), the JSON-mode payload is wrapped:"},"4120":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-52","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#metadata-envelope","content":"iggy_id is a 32-character lowercase hex string (no dashes)."},"4121":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-53","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#metadata-envelope","content":"Set include_metadata = false to send the payload without wrapping (useful when the downstream service expects bare JSON, e.g. Slack webhooks)."},"4122":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-54","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#metadata-envelope","content":"Non-JSON payloads (raw, flatbuffer, proto, and avro schemas) cannot be embedded in a JSON body directly, so they are base64-encoded with an explicit marker:"},"4123":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-55","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#metadata-envelope","content":"With the envelope enabled, this object becomes the payload field shown above."},"4124":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-56","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#metadata-envelope","content":"The connector doesn't require any particular message structure on input. The envelope is applied on the way out, not expected on the way in, so your producers can publish whatever they like."},"4125":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-57","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#authentication","content":"The HTTP sink supports authentication via custom headers under [plugin_config.headers]. All headers are sent with every request, including health checks."},"4126":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-58","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#authentication","content":"Any header works the same way: use x-api-key = \"my-secret-api-key\" for API-key schemes, or Authorization = \"Basic dXNlcjpwYXNzd29yZA==\" (base64 of username:password) for basic auth. Multiple headers are combined per request. For secrets, prefer environment variable overrides at the process level (see the upstream README) to keep tokens out of config.toml."},"4127":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-59","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#retry--delivery-semantics","content":"Failed requests are retried with exponential backoff: retry_delay, multiplied by retry_backoff_multiplier per attempt, capped at max_retry_delay, for up to max_retries attempts."},"4128":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-60","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#retry--delivery-semantics","content":"Transient errors (retried): network errors, HTTP 429, 500, 502, 503, 504."},"4129":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-61","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#retry--delivery-semantics","content":"Non-transient errors (fail immediately): HTTP 400, 401, 403, 404, 405, etc."},"4130":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-62","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#retry--delivery-semantics","content":"success_status_codes (default [200, 201, 202, 204]) short-circuits retries: any status code in this set is treated as success and is never retried, even codes that are normally transient. Placing 429 in the set makes the sink accept rate-limited responses as delivered. The sink warns at startup about such overlaps."},"4131":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-63","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#retry--delivery-semantics","content":"HTTP 429 Retry-After: the header is logged but not honored. Retry timing always uses the computed backoff."},"4132":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-64","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#retry--delivery-semantics","content":"Partial delivery (individual/raw modes): after a fixed number of consecutive HTTP failures (3 at the time of writing, not configurable), the remainder of the batch is aborted to avoid hammering a dead endpoint."},"4133":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-65","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#retry--delivery-semantics","content":"The connector runtime commits consumer-group offsets when messages are polled, before consume() runs, and doesn't inspect its return value, so the effective delivery guarantee is at-most-once at the runtime level. The sink's internal retry loop provides best-effort delivery within each consume() call."},"4134":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-66","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#webhook-slack","content":"The sink performs no outbound payload transformation. include_metadata = false only skips the envelope. The message payload is delivered exactly as produced, so your producer must publish JSON already in the shape Slack expects (for example {\"text\": \"...\"})."},"4135":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-67","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#deployment--performance","content":"One iggy-connectors runtime process can host many connectors: the local config provider imports every connector TOML file under its config_dir, and each entry gets its own plugin instance and consume tasks in the same process. Each connector entry has exactly one [plugin_config] block and therefore one destination URL. To send to multiple destinations, add multiple HTTP sink entries with distinct keys and URLs (in the same runtime or separate ones). For fan-out from a single topic to multiple endpoints, point multiple sink entries at the same topic with different consumer_group names so each maintains its own offset."},"4136":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-68","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#deployment--performance","content":"Throughput is dominated by batch-mode choice: the runtime calls consume() sequentially within each topic task, so individual and raw modes perform N round trips per poll cycle while ndjson/json_array collapse the same batch into one request. Connection pooling and HTTP keep-alive are enabled by default. Tune max_connections and batch_length together for high-throughput targets."},"4137":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-69","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#deployment--performance","content":"For multi-instance deployment patterns (Docker, Kubernetes, fan-out topologies), connection pool tuning, and full performance analysis, see the upstream http_sink README."},"4138":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-70","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#known-limitations","content":"No Retry-After honoring: the header is logged but doesn't influence retry timing."},"4139":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-71","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#known-limitations","content":"No dead-letter queue: failed messages are logged at error! level but not persisted."},"4140":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-72","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#known-limitations","content":"No request signing: AWS SigV4, HMAC, and similar schemes aren't supported. Use custom headers or a signing proxy."},"4141":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-73","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#known-limitations","content":"No per-topic URL routing: all topics in one connector instance share the same url. For routing, deploy multiple instances."},"4142":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-74","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#known-limitations","content":"No OAuth2 / OIDC token refresh: bearer tokens are static. Use an auth proxy for services that require token rotation."},"4143":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-75","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#known-limitations","content":"No mTLS client certificates: terminate mTLS at a sidecar proxy for production use."},"4144":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-76","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#known-limitations","content":"Plaintext secrets in config: header values are stored verbatim in config.toml. Use environment variable overrides at the process level for sensitive values."},"4145":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http-77","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/http#known-limitations","content":"For the complete list and implementation context, see the upstream http_sink README."},"4146":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","type":"page","content":"Iceberg Sink","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Connectors","Sinks"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg"},"4147":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-0","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","content":"Consume messages from Iggy topics and store them in Iceberg tables, with REST catalogs and S3-compatible storage."},"4148":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-1","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#features","content":"Features"},"4149":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-2","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#configuration-example","content":"Configuration example"},"4150":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-3","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#configuration-options","content":"Configuration Options"},"4151":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-4","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#dynamic-routing","content":"Dynamic Routing"},"4152":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-5","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#dynamic-routing-configuration-example","content":"Dynamic routing configuration example"},"4153":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-6","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#source-compatibility","content":"Source Compatibility"},"4154":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-7","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","content":"The Iceberg Sink Connector allows you to consume messages from Iggy topics and store them in Iceberg tables."},"4155":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-8","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#features","content":"Support for S3-compatible storage"},"4156":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-9","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#features","content":"Support for REST catalogs"},"4157":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-10","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#features","content":"Single destination table"},"4158":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-11","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#features","content":"Multiple-table fan-out static routing"},"4159":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-12","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#features","content":"Multiple-table fan-out dynamic routing"},"4160":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-13","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#configuration-options","content":"tables: The names of the Iceberg tables you want to statically route Iggy messages to. The name should include the table’s namespace, separated by a dot (.)."},"4161":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-14","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#configuration-options","content":"catalog_type: The type of catalog you are routing data to. Currently, only REST catalogs are fully supported."},"4162":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-15","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#configuration-options","content":"warehouse: The name of the bucket or warehouse where Iggy will upload data files."},"4163":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-16","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#configuration-options","content":"uri: The URI of the Iceberg catalog."},"4164":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-17","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#configuration-options","content":"dynamic_routing: Enables dynamic routing. See more details later in this document."},"4165":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-18","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#configuration-options","content":"dynamic_route_field: The name of the message field that specifies the Iceberg table to route data to. See more details below."},"4166":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-19","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#configuration-options","content":"store_url: The URL of the object storage for data uploads."},"4167":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-20","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#configuration-options","content":"store_access_key_id: The access key ID of the object storage."},"4168":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-21","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#configuration-options","content":"store_secret_access_key: The secret key used to upload data to the object storage."},"4169":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-22","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#configuration-options","content":"store_region: The region of the object storage. Required. For S3-compatible stores that ignore it, supply any placeholder value."},"4170":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-23","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#configuration-options","content":"store_class: The storage class to use. Currently, only S3-compatible storage is supported."},"4171":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-24","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#dynamic-routing","content":"If you don't know the names of the Iceberg tables you want to route data to in advance, you can use the dynamic routing feature.\nInsert a field in your Iggy messages with the name of the Iceberg table the message should be routed to. The Iggy connector will parse this field at runtime and route the message to the correct table."},"4172":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-25","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#dynamic-routing","content":"The Iggy Iceberg Connector will skip messages in the following cases:"},"4173":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-26","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#dynamic-routing","content":"The table declared in the message field does not exist."},"4174":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-27","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#dynamic-routing","content":"The message does not contain the field specified in the dynamic_route_field configuration option."},"4175":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-28","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#dynamic-routing-configuration-example","content":"Transforms are declared at the top level of the connector file, next to [plugin_config], and every [transforms.*] section requires enabled = true. See the transforms documentation for details."},"4176":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-29","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#dynamic-routing-configuration-example","content":"Note: The value in the message field must contain both the namespace and the table name, separated by a dot (.).\nExample:"},"4177":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-30","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#dynamic-routing-configuration-example","content":"Namespace: nyc"},"4178":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-31","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#dynamic-routing-configuration-example","content":"Table name: users"},"4179":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-32","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#source-compatibility","content":"The Iceberg sink expects flat JSON where each top-level key maps directly to a column in the target Iceberg table schema. Sources that wrap row data in an envelope (with metadata fields alongside a nested data object) are not directly compatible: the Arrow JSON reader will map envelope keys to table columns, producing nulls or schema errors."},"4180":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-33","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#source-compatibility","content":"If your source emits envelope-wrapped JSON, use the unwrap_envelope transform to extract the inner data field before it reaches the sink:"},"4181":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg-34","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/iceberg#source-compatibility","content":"Set field to the envelope key that holds the row data. See the transforms documentation and your source connector's documentation for details on the envelope shape."},"4182":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","type":"page","content":"InfluxDB Sink","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Connectors","Sinks"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb"},"4183":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-0","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","content":"Write messages from Iggy streams to InfluxDB as line-protocol points, on both InfluxDB V2 and V3."},"4184":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-1","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"4185":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-2","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#common-options","content":"Common Options"},"4186":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-3","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#payload-formats","content":"Payload Formats"},"4187":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-4","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#reliability","content":"Reliability"},"4188":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-5","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#transforms","content":"Transforms"},"4189":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-6","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","content":"The InfluxDB sink connector consumes messages from Iggy streams and writes them to InfluxDB as line-protocol points. It supports both InfluxDB V2 (OSS 2.x / Cloud) and InfluxDB V3 (Core / Enterprise), selected with the version option."},"4190":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-7","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","content":"This page is a curated subset of the documentation. The canonical reference is the upstream influxdb_sink README in the apache/iggy repository."},"4191":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-8","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#configuration","content":"InfluxDB V2 organizes data as org + bucket. V3 uses a single db field instead. Omitting version defaults to \"v2\" for backward compatibility. The write body