s","content":"Messages per write request"},"4232":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-49","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#common-options","content":"payload_format"},"4233":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-50","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#common-options","content":"string"},"4234":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-51","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#common-options","content":"json"},"4235":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-52","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#common-options","content":"json, text, or base64"},"4236":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-53","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#common-options","content":"include_metadata"},"4237":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-54","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#common-options","content":"bool"},"4238":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-55","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#common-options","content":"true"},"4239":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-56","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#common-options","content":"Inject stream/topic/partition fields into each point (the offset tag is always written regardless)"},"4240":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-57","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#common-options","content":"The include_checksum, include_origin_timestamp, include_stream_tag, include_topic_tag, and include_partition_tag flags also default to true. Disable them individually to slim down points. Resilience options cover timeout (30s), max_retries (3), retry_delay / retry_max_delay, startup health-check retries, and a circuit breaker (circuit_breaker_threshold 5, circuit_breaker_cool_down 30s). See the upstream influxdb_sink README for the full list."},"4241":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-58","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#payload-formats","content":"json (default): the message payload is validated as JSON, compact-serialized, and written as a single payload_json string field (individual JSON fields do not become separate field entries)."},"4242":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-59","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#payload-formats","content":"text: the payload is written as a single payload_text string field."},"4243":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-60","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#payload-formats","content":"base64: the raw payload bytes are base64-encoded into a payload_base64 string field."},"4244":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-61","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#payload-formats","content":"An unrecognized payload_format logs a warning and falls back to json."},"4245":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-62","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#reliability","content":"Messages are serialized to line protocol and each polled batch is split into chunks of at most batch_size messages, one HTTP POST per chunk. Transient errors (429 and 5xx) are retried with exponential backoff, and after circuit_breaker_threshold consecutive failures the connector stops issuing writes until the cool-down window elapses, then probes again. The startup health check retries with its own backoff, so the connector tolerates InfluxDB starting after it."},"4246":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb-63","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/influxdb#transforms","content":"Transforms can be applied before writing to InfluxDB. See the transforms documentation for the available types and their configuration."},"4247":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","type":"page","content":"Meilisearch Sink","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Connectors","Sinks"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch"},"4248":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-0","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","content":"Index messages from Iggy streams as documents in a Meilisearch index through the official Rust SDK."},"4249":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-1","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"4250":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-2","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#common-options","content":"Common Options"},"4251":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-3","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#document-mapping","content":"Document Mapping"},"4252":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-4","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#delivery-semantics","content":"Delivery Semantics"},"4253":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-5","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#transforms","content":"Transforms"},"4254":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-6","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","content":"The Meilisearch sink connector consumes messages from Iggy streams and indexes them as documents in a Meilisearch index through the official Rust SDK. It can create the index on startup and waits for Meilisearch indexing tasks to complete by default, so task failures surface as connector errors."},"4255":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-7","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","content":"This page is a curated subset of the documentation. The canonical reference is the upstream meilisearch_sink README in the apache/iggy repository."},"4256":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-8","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#common-options","content":"Option"},"4257":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-9","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#common-options","content":"Type"},"4258":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-10","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#common-options","content":"Default"},"4259":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-11","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#common-options","content":"Description"},"4260":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-12","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#common-options","content":"url"},"4261":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-13","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/