age_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#common-options","content":"Request timeout"},"4300":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-52","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#common-options","content":"Further options cover task polling (task_timeout 30s, task_poll_interval 100ms) and transient retries (max_retries 3, retry_delay 500ms, max_retry_delay 5s, max_open_retries 5). See the upstream meilisearch_sink README for details."},"4301":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-53","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#document-mapping","content":"JSON object payloads are indexed as documents directly. JSON arrays and scalars are wrapped in a value field, since Meilisearch documents must be objects. Raw payloads are parsed as JSON when possible and otherwise indexed as base64 data. Text payloads land in a text field. Records with unsupported payload schemas are skipped with a warning and counted as errors."},"4302":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-54","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#document-mapping","content":"When the configured primary key is absent from a document, the connector injects a stable value derived from the stream, topic, partition, offset, and message ID, avoiding Meilisearch primary-key inference failures. If your payloads carry their own primary key, its values must be unique. Otherwise add-or-replace semantics collapse distinct messages into one document."},"4303":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-55","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#document-mapping","content":"With include_metadata = true, reserved iggy_* fields (stream, topic, partition, offset, checksum, timestamps) are written after payload parsing and overwrite same-named payload fields."},"4304":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-56","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#delivery-semantics","content":"The runtime commits consumer offsets when messages are polled and doesn't gate commits on consume()'s result, so the effective guarantee is at-most-once on sink errors. The retry settings provide best-effort retries within a single batch. Setting wait_for_tasks = false makes indexing fire-and-forget: submission succeeds before Meilisearch confirms indexing, and later task failures are neither observed nor retried."},"4305":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch-57","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/meilisearch#transforms","content":"Transforms can be applied before indexing into Meilisearch. See the transforms documentation for the available types and their configuration."},"4306":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","type":"page","content":"MongoDB Sink","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","Connectors","Sinks"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb"},"4307":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-0","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","content":"Insert messages from Iggy streams into a MongoDB collection, one document per message."},"4308":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-1","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"4309":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-2","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#plugin-config-options","content":"Plugin config options"},"4310":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-3","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#transforms","content":"Transforms"},"4311":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-4","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","content":"The MongoDB sink connector writes messages from Iggy streams to a MongoDB database. Each message is inserted as a document into the configured collection."},"4312":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-5","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#plugin-config-options","content":"Option"},"4313":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-6","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#plugin-config-options","content":"Type"},"4314":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-7","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#plugin-config-options","content":"Default"},"4315":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-8","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#plugin-config-options","content":"Description"},"4316":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-9","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#plugin-config-options","content":"connection_uri"},"4317":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-10","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#plugin-config-options","content":"string"},"4318":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-11","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#plugin-config-options","content":"required"},"4319":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb-12","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/mongodb#pl