":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-52","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"payload_format"},"4629":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-53","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"string"},"4630":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-54","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"auto"},"4631":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-55","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"auto, json, text, base64, or binary (alias for base64)"},"4632":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-56","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"include_metadata"},"4633":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-57","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"bool"},"4634":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-58","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"true"},"4635":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-59","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"Store stream/topic/partition/offset/timestamp/schema fields"},"4636":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-60","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#common-options","content":"The include_headers, include_checksum, and include_origin_timestamp flags also default to true. Retry and timeout options: query_timeout (30s), max_retries (3 total attempts), retry_delay (100ms), max_retry_delay (5s), plus verbose_logging. See the upstream surrealdb_sink README for the full table."},"4637":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-61","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#stored-shape","content":"With metadata enabled, each record contains the deterministic id, the iggy_message_id, provenance fields (iggy_stream, iggy_topic, iggy_partition_id, iggy_offset, iggy_timestamp, iggy_origin_timestamp, iggy_checksum, iggy_schema), iggy_headers, the payload, and its payload_encoding. With payload_format = \"auto\", JSON payloads are stored as queryable SurrealDB values, text payloads as strings, and binary payloads as base64 strings."},"4638":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-62","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#delivery-semantics","content":"The runtime commits consumer offsets before consume() runs, so persistent write failures are at-most-once: they are logged but not redelivered. Transient failures are retried inside the batch with capped exponential backoff. Because records use deterministic ids and INSERT IGNORE, a replayed batch (for example after a connector restart re-reads uncommitted messages) doesn't create duplicates."},"4639":{"id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb-63","page_id":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/connectors/sinks/surrealdb#transforms","content":"Transforms can be applied before writing to SurrealDB. See the transforms documentation for the available types and their configuration."},"4640":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","type":"page","content":"C++ SDK (WIP)","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","SDK","C++"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro"},"4641":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-0","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","content":"The C++ SDK, a CXX bridge over the Rust SDK, and how to build it from source with Bazel."},"4642":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-1","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#building-from-source","content":"Building from source"},"4643":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-2","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#quick-start","content":"Quick start"},"4644":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-3","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#connection-strings","content":"Connection strings"},"4645":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-4","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#helper-types","content":"Helper types"},"4646":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-5","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#current-status","content":"Current status"},"4647":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-6","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","content":"The Iggy C++ SDK wraps the Rust SDK through a CXX FFI bridge, so it can use all transport protocols (TCP, QUIC, HTTP, WebSocket) via connection strings. The source code is available at github.com/apache/iggy/tree/master/foreign/cpp."},"4648":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-7","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","content":"This SDK isn't published to any package registry. Consume it from the monorepo and build it from source with Bazel."},"4649":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-8","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#building-from-source","content":"The project builds with Bazel (BUILD.bazel / MODULE.bazel). The build drives the system-provided cargo toolchain to compile the Rust bridge, so concurrent runs can race. Run builds serially."},"4650":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-9","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#quick-start","content":"The snippet below mirrors the SDK's own end-to-end tests in foreign/cpp/tests/e2e:"},"4651":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-10","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#quick-start","content":"Polling strategies are selected by kind string: offset, timestamp, first, last, or next. Partitioning kinds for sending are balanced, partition_id, and messages_key."},"4652":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-11","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#connection-strings","content":"The C++ SDK supports the same connection string format as the Rust SDK:"},"4653":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-12","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#connection-strings","content":"When an empty string or plain address is passed to new_connection(), it defaults to TCP."},"4654":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-13","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#helper-types","content":"Beyond the generated lib.rs.h FFI surface, foreign/cpp/include/iggy.hpp ships typed C++ helpers: CompressionAlgorithm, MaxTopicSize, Expiry, PollingStrategy, IdKind, TopicOption, SnapshotCompression, and SystemSnapshotType, plus the IggyException error type. They construct and validate the kind strings and values the raw FFI calls expect."},"4655":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-14","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#current-status","content":"The FFI bridge exposes the full command-level client: streams, topics, partitions, and segments; message sending and polling with user headers; consumer groups and consumer offsets; stats, client info, and cluster metadata; snapshots; permission updates and password changes; topic option discovery (describe_options); and raw binary requests (send_binary_request)."},"4656":{"id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro-15","page_id":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/cpp/intro#current-status","content":"Not yet exposed: the high-level Producer/Consumer wrappers and user management (create/get/update/delete users, personal access tokens). Contributions are welcome."},"4657":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","type":"page","content":"Examples","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","SDK","C#"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples"},"4658":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-0","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","content":"Producer and consumer samples for the C# SDK, built on the high-level publisher and consumer."},"4659":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-1","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#producer","content":"Producer"},"4660":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-2","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#consumer-group","content":"Consumer group"},"4661":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-3","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#typed-messages","content":"Typed messages"},"4662":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-4","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#more-examples","content":"More examples"},"4663":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-5","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","content":"These samples use the High-level SDK - the recommended way to build producers and consumers. For the low-level, per-call equivalents, see the Guide."},"4664":{"id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples-6","page_id":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/csharp/examples#producer","content":"A publisher that creates the stream and topic if missing, batches sends in the background, and retries failures:"},"4665"