ike the producer, the consumer must stay a mutable binding for its whole life: init() takes &mut self, and next() comes from the futures Stream implementation which also requires mutable access. The init() is used to ensure that the consumer is ready to receive the messages by validating the existence of the stream, topic, consumer group etc. Here's how you can consume the messages:"},"5376":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk-64","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk#consumer","content":"In order to use the async iterator extension, add futures-util dependency and import futures_util::StreamExt."},"5377":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk-65","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk#consumer-builder-options","content":"Defaults and lesser-known knobs on IggyConsumerBuilder:"},"5378":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk-66","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk#consumer-builder-options","content":"Option"},"5379":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk-67","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk#consumer-builder-options","content":"Default"},"5380":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk-68","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk#consumer-builder-options","content":"Description"},"5381":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk-69","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk#consumer-builder-options","content":"polling_strategy(...)"},"5382":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk-70","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk#consumer-builder-options","content":"next()"},"5383":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk-71","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/hi