nvalidCommand, use login_user/logout_user so the SDK session state stays correct. Custom codes are forwarded to the server, which decides whether it implements them."},"5436":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk-124","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/high-level-sdk#raw-requests","content":"send_http_request(method, path, body) invokes an arbitrary HTTP endpoint and returns the raw response body. HTTP transport only. Binary transports return FeatureUnavailable."},"5437":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","type":"page","content":"Intro","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","SDK","Rust"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro"},"5438":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-0","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","content":"The Rust SDK, the primary and most complete Iggy client, and where its source lives."},"5439":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-1","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"5440":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-2","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#high-level-vs-low-level-api","content":"High-level vs low-level API"},"5441":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-3","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#connection-string","content":"Connection string"},"5442":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-4","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#quick-example","content":"Quick example"},"5443":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-5","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","content":"The Rust SDK is the primary and most feature-complete client for Iggy. It is available on crates.io and the source code is part of the core repository."},"5444":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-6","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#prerequisites","content":"The examples below log in with the iggy/iggy root credentials, which only exist when the server is started with the default-credentials flag (or IGGY_ROOT_USERNAME/IGGY_ROOT_PASSWORD set) on its first boot. Otherwise root gets a generated password and the examples fail with InvalidCredentials:"},"5445":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-7","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#prerequisites","content":"--fresh wipes the local data directory. This setup is for development only."},"5446":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-8","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#high-level-vs-low-level-api","content":"The SDK provides two layers:"},"5447":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-9","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#high-level-vs-low-level-api","content":"High-level API (recommended) - the easiest way to get started. It handles connection management, auto-batching, consumer group lifecycle, offset commits, retry logic, and reconnection out of the box. Use IggyClient, IggyProducer, and IggyConsumer for the best developer experience."},"5448":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-10","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#high-level-vs-low-level-api","content":"Low-level API - direct access to individual protocol operations. Useful when you need fine-grained control over every request, or when building custom abstractions on top."},"5449":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-11","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#high-level-vs-low-level-api","content":"The high-level API is built on top of the low-level one, so you can always drop down when needed."},"5450":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-12","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#connection-string","content":"The connection string is the simplest way to configure the client. It supports all four transport protocols:"},"5451":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-13","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#connection-string","content":"Options can be appended as query parameters:"},"5452":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-14","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#connection-string","content":"Personal Access Tokens are also supported. Any credential without a colon is treated as a PAT. Paste the token exactly as the server returned it, with no prefix:"},"5453":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-15","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#connection-string","content":"See Connection Strings for the full per-transport option tables and defaults."},"5454":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-16","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#quick-example","content":"Partition IDs are 0-based: the first partition of a topic is partition 0."},"5455":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro-17","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/intro#quick-example","content":"For the full getting started tutorial, see Getting Started. For the high-level producer/consumer builders, see High-level SDK and Stream Builder."},"5456":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/stream-builder","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/stream-builder","type":"page","content":"Stream Builder","breadcrumbs":["Documentation","SDK","Rust"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/sdk/rust/stream-builder"},"5457":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/stream-builder-0","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/stream-builder","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/sdk/rust/stream-builder","content":"The stream builder, for event-driven applications that would otherwise repeat producer and consumer setup."},"5458":{"id":"/docs/sdk/rust/stream-builder-1","page_id":"/docs/sdk/rust/stream-builder","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"