[4874,"int"],[4968,"int"],[4993,"int"],[4997,"int"],[614,"Int128"],[602,"Int16"],[606,"Int32"],[610,"Int64"],[598,"Int8"],[3586,"integer"],[4053,"integer"],[4057,"integer"],[523,"Integer order equals semver order. The value tracks the iggy_binary_protocol crate release. Under 0.x the compatibility gate is minor-scoped: the server accepts a client whose packed version is at least the server's minimum and whose major.minor is at most the server's. Patch releases never change the wire, so the upper bound ignores patch. Past 1.0.0 the gate follows strict semver (major bump = incompatible)."],[615,"Integers are little-endian. Bool is one byte."],[1752,"Internally, dlopen2 provides a safe and efficient way of loading the plugins via C FFI."],[2963,"interval"],[2972,"interval"],[3799,"interval"],[5003,"Interval at which pending messages are flushed"],[3075,"Interval between outbound reconnect attempts to peers."],[4741,"Interval between the automatic pings the TCP client sends while connected (see Heartbeat). Init-only; must be between 1 millisecond and about 49 days"],[5422,"Interval(d)"],[5426,"IntervalOrAfter(d, after)"],[5388,"IntervalOrWhen(1s, PollingMessages)"],[5424,"IntervalOrWhen(d, when)"],[5437,"Intro"],[34,"Introduction"],[1639,"Introduction"],[2431,"Introduction"],[3199,"Introduction"],[197,"Invalid sentinel"],[1078,"InvalidCredentials"],[1066,"InvalidRequestBody"],[1069,"InvalidRequestBodySize"],[1063,"InvalidRequestOperation"],[1081,"InvalidToken"],[2077,"io_uring and compio"],[2104,"io_uring is completion-based - you submit I/O requests to a submission queue (SQ), and the kernel completes them and places results in a completion queue (CQ). Both queues are lock-free ring buffers shared between user space and kernel. This is fundamentally better for disk I/O."],[4078,"IoT / Sensor Relay (binary payloads)"],[1432,"ip"],[1491,"ip is not the bind interface for the client transports. tcp, quic, http, and websocket bind whatever their own address settings say. The roster supplies only their ports. The defaults bind loopback, so a cluster spread across hosts needs each transport's address set to 0.0.0.0 or the routable interface. The server warns at startup when a bind cannot serve the advertised ip."],[1534,"ip must be a literal IP address. Use advertised_address when clients can't reach it (see Configuration)"],[4880,"IReadOnlyList<RentedMessageResponse>"],[2703,"issuer"],[2705,"Issuer claim of minted tokens."],[2736,"issuer, audience, and jwks_url are required per entry. user_id is the non-zero iggy user every token from that issuer is remapped onto. It defaults to 0 (root), which is rejected, so set it explicitly."],[2711,"Issuers accepted during validation."],[4555,"It's also important to note, that the supported format(s) might vary depending on the connector implementation. For example, you might expect JSON as the payload format, which can be then easily parsed and processed by upstream components such as data transforms, but at the same time, you could support the other formats and let the user decide which one to use."],[3853,"It's also important to note, that the supported format(s) might vary depending on the connector implementation. For example, you might use JSON as the payload format, which can be then easily parsed and processed by downstream components such as data transforms, but at the same time, you could support the other formats and let the user decide which one to use."],[1411,"Java"],[2028,"Java"],[2454,"Java"],[5174,"Java SDK"],[496,"Join consumer group. Code: 604."],[5392,"Join the consumer group automatically"],[835,"JoinConsumerGroup"],[4704,"Joining and leaving"],[178,"Journal repair"],[257,"Journal repair: request an op range"],[3035,"journal_slots"],[3449,"journal.wal: the prepare journal. Each entry is a 256-byte PrepareHeader (the consensus header carrying checksums, view, op and commit numbers, operation discriminant, and acting user) followed by the operation's wire-format body, exactly as