eserves each segment's bytes up front on filesystems that support it. See Topic options."],[2647,"segment_size topic option"],[3501,"segment_size x partitions at most 64 GiB per create"],[2511,"SegmentClient - delete segments"],[3386,"Segmented log"],[430,"Segments"],[3403,"Segments store batch records, not individual messages. The record is byte-identical to the wire encoding: the one layout a SendMessages body, the replicated prepare, the persisted segment record, and the poll reply all share. There is no other message encoding."],[3214,"Select this node's entry in cluster.nodes. Required when cluster.enabled = true. See Clustering."],[2777,"self_signed"],[2820,"self_signed"],[2863,"self_signed"],[2878,"self_signed = true always generates an ephemeral certificate and ignores configured files."],[2876,"self_signed = true generates an ephemeral certificate only while cert_file does not exist; an existing PEM pair is loaded instead."],[3281,"self_signed = true generates an ephemeral certificate only while cert_file does not exist; an existing PEM pair is loaded instead."],[3365,"self_signed = true generates an ephemeral certificate only while cert_file does not exist; an existing PEM pair is loaded instead."],[3349,"Self-service: an authenticated user can always read their own account, change their own password, and manage their own personal access tokens, without any of the user permissions above."],[1566,"Self-signed mode (self_signed = true): the node auto-generates a certificate at boot and the dialer accepts ANY peer certificate. This gives you encrypted replica traffic without certificate management, but no acceptor authentication at all: peer authenticity rests entirely on the PSK handshake. Use CA mode when the replica network is not trusted."],[620,"Semantics:"],[4737,"Send buffer size in bytes"],[5316,"Send confirmations"],[3345,"Send messages"],[117,"Send messages (partitioning: balanced, key, partition)"],[1259,"Send messages from a binary file written by