local_data. The chart supplies IGGY_NODE_ADVERTISED_ADDRESS as the in-cluster Service DNS name; override it with server.advertisedAddress when clients arrive through a LoadBalancer or an Ingress. Images that predate the setting, including the 0.7.0 pinned by default, log the variable as unknown and start anyway."],[4778,"Server name for the TLS handshake"],[3192,"Server Service - exposes the http (3000), quic (8080), and tcp (8090) ports. WebSocket is not exposed by the chart."],[67,"Server statistics (streams, topics, partitions, OS info)"],[216,"server to client"],[236,"server to client"],[656,"server to client"],[660,"server to client"],[859,"Server to client. 256 bytes, followed by size - 256 bytes of body."],[975,"Server to client. 256 bytes, never a body. An eviction is session-terminal: it says \"this session is dead\", carries no per-request correlation, and a client should deinitialize and re-login."],[1031,"server_protocol_version"],[1036,"server_protocol_version_min"],[4846,"Server-assigned ids are 0-based: the first stream, topic, partition, or consumer group gets id 0. The root user has id 0 as well."],[2180,"Server-assigned timestamp"],[1997,"Server-side storage of consumer offsets"],[1127,"Server-stamped at admission. Producers send zero."],[1137,"Server-stamped at journal append (microseconds). Producers send zero."],[1132,"Server-stamped when the batch is appended to the partition journal. Producers send zero."],[167,"Server-to-server"],[1112,"Server-to-server: prepare/ack replication, view changes, and state transfer."],[2983,"service_name"],[3196,"ServiceAccount, HPA, Ingress - the usual optional plumbing, for both server and UI."],[3197,"ServiceMonitor - Prometheus scrape config (optional). The /metrics endpoint requires a bearer credential like every other read, so wire a token (e.g. a personal access token stored in a Secret) into server.serviceMonitor.authorization - an unauthenticated scrape gets 401."],[260,"serving peer to requester"],[264,"serving peer to requester"],[268,"serving peer to requester"],[747,"session"],[773,"session (code 39)"],[767,"session (login handshake, codes 40 and 45)"],[1076,"Session bound to a different release"],[1073,"Session epoch below the cluster's retained minimum"],[749,"Session fence epoch from the login reply. Zero on the login-register request itself and on non-replicated operations sent before login (only PING is accepted unauthenticated)."],[180,"Session forwarding"],[661,"Session is dead, no per-request correlation"],[858,"session is the fence epoch: the value handed back by the login reply. Every request after login must echo it. When the same client id registers again, the new registration mints a higher epoch and requests carrying the old one are fenced (rejected as zombies)."],[4907,"Session-control codes (login, logout, and the like) are rejected with an invalid-command error, and the operation is TCP-only: HTTP clients throw FeatureUnavailableException."],[1088,"Session-level failure"],[1087,"SessionError"],[1075,"SessionReleaseMismatch"],[1072,"SessionTooLow"],[1786,"Set active sink version: PUT {base_url}/sinks/{key}/configs/active"],[1787,"Set active source version: PUT {base_url}/sources/{key}/configs/active"],[1690,"Set environment variable IGGY_CONNECTORS_CONFIG_PATH=core/connectors/runtime/example_config/config.toml (adjust the path as needed) pointing to the runtime configuration file."],[4181,"Set field to the envelope key that holds the row data. See the transforms documentation and your source connector's documentation for details on the envelope shape."],[2630,"Set IGGY_ROOT_USERNAME and IGGY_ROOT_PASSWORD to iggy unless they are already present in the environment. Only the first creation of the root user reads these values. Development only."],[4837,"Set IggyClientConfigurator.MessageEncryptor to encrypt message payloads and user headers client-side - they are encrypted on send and decrypted on poll, so the server only ever sees ciphertext. The 